# Boost on 37 (Karen)'s end save (run.py hgss_boost: np_save4 heal-party).
# The Elite Four's rooms lead one into the next with no Pokemon Center between (the way back shuts behind
# the player: scr_seq_0820_T10R0201.s:22-36), where a player uses Full Restores and Revives; no bot uses items.
# party-heal stands in for them: HP, status and PP as a Pokemon Center leaves them. The first chained run
# reached Bruno with all but Pelipper fainted after Will and Koga, and whited out in four turns.
party-heal
# Lance (GYARADOS 46, DRAGONITE 49 x2, AERODACTYL 48, CHARIZARD 48, DRAGONITE 50) beat the healed party in the first
# chained run: Ampharos's Thunderbolts are resisted by the Dragonite, and the two Ice Beam users ran dry on them.
# Levels (np_save4 set-level) for the champion and Ice coverage: PELIPPER's Whirlpool (no whirlpool after the den,
# 28) -> Blizzard again (TM14).
party-move 4 3 MOVE_BLIZZARD
party-level 0 62
party-level 2 60
party-level 3 64
party-level 4 62
party-level 5 64
# The second run with those lost the same way: the lead TYPHLOSION had only Fire and Normal moves into Gyarados and
# the Dragonite. TYPHLOSION: SmokeScreen -> Rock Slide (TM80; TYPHLOSION tms include 80), super effective on all
# of Lance's flyers, Ember -> Focus Blast (TM52).
party-move 0 2 MOVE_ROCK_SLIDE
party-move 0 3 MOVE_FOCUS_BLAST
# A third run with Rock Slide lost too (4 Rock Slides into an Intimidated Gyarados, the Dragonite's Thunder Wave):
# auto_battle neither switches for a matchup nor uses items, so the levels go past the champion's instead
# (above: TYPHLOSION 62, SCYTHER 60, AMPHAROS 64, PELIPPER 62, FERALIGATR 64).
